// **The pond an animal can walk into** -- and, measured, the first bed in
// which water is allowed to be a barrier at all.
//
// Every other pond in `assets/lab_scenarios/` is a stone box with vertical
// walls: `the_pond`, `the_pond_sediment`, `the_pond_stocked`,
// `the_pond_shore`. **That wall is why four separate instruments reported
// that a pond is indistinguishable from the same hole left dry** -- colony
// survival, births, `creature_arena arm=lethal` and `labforage`. A vertical
// stone face stops an ant at the rim, so whatever stands at the bottom of the
// pit never gets a chance to matter, and water-against-dry reads null for a
// reason that has nothing to do with water.
//
// **Give the ants a bank they can walk down and the water is what stops
// them**, because it is the only thing left to stop them. Columns the colony
// ever occupied, `labforage`, six seeds, 24,000 frames, one binary
// (`Reports/aquatic-implementation-plan-2026-09-14.md` §1.11):
//
//     no pit at all            279.5
//     this bowl, DRY           254.5
//     this bowl, WITH WATER    205.0     <- 49.5 columns, 6 of 6 seeds separated
//     vertical basin, water    199.5
//     vertical basin, dry      196.5     <- the same water costs NOTHING here
//
// **Two things in the shape are load-bearing and neither is decoration.**
//
// *The stone is a liner, not a wedge.* Stone is unavoidable -- §1.5 measured
// the bed's own 96-row soil column having **exactly** enough unsaturated room
// to swallow a pond of this size, so a soil-lined basin drains to zero by
// frame 4,000. But the seal only has to be one tread thick. The first sloped
// version filled the whole wedge with stone and rendered as a concrete tank;
// this one lines the bowl and leaves the bed's own soil as the visible bank,
// which is what makes it read as a pond.
//
// *The steps are 2 rows by 4 columns, and the row count is the number that
// matters.* What an ant climbs is a step, not an average gradient, so the
// step height is kept small rather than the slope made shallow.
//
// Holds: ~3,001 water cells resting on water at frame 16,000 against an
// initial bowl volume of 2,944.
//
// **This is the Phase 2 bed.** A swim verb raced in any of the four boxed
// ponds would be raced against a wall.
(
    name: "the_pond_bowl",
    title: "THE POND, WITH A BANK",
    question: "A pond with a bank an ant can walk down -- does the water itself now cost the colony anything, where a walled basin said it cost nothing?",
